From 892f204dfc2900b874d01cdd842a3bfef1d6c9b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henk Wiedig <henk@wiedig.de>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:26:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] drm/bridge: it66121: IT66122 with YCbCr 4:2:2 input

The SinYine F1 VRX's HDMI transmitter is an IT66122 (vendor 0x4954,
device byte 0x22) on a 16-bit YCbCr 4:2:2 bus with separate syncs. From
its stock driver (libpn_hdmitx_it6612x.so, ITE's reference code, run
under qemu against a modelled chip):

- "ite,it66122": after the reset, 30 ms, then ITE's init table as that
  driver has it (register, mask, value); the IT66121 paths otherwise
  (clock bank, AFE)
- bus-width 16: input mode YUV422 with input clock delay 1 (reg 0x70
  0x41), YUV->RGB CSC with its ITU601 matrix, which keeps the VO's full
  range, and a full-range AVI infoframe as stock sends; input bus
  format UYVY8_1X16
- the IT66122's AFE extras above 20 MHz (0x61 bit 1, 0x63, 0x66) and
  the CSC register's bit 5, as stock writes them
- ite,force-hpd: the connector is always connected (PixelPilot wants a
  connected one) and without a sink's EDID the modes are 1080p60,
  720p60, 1080p50 and 720p50 from a built-in EDID; no IRQ line is wired,
  the chip is polled

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c | 182 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 172 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

